  "ingredients": [
    "1 cup white sugar",
    "0.5 cup light corn syrup",
    "0.25 cup water",
    "0.25 teaspoon salt",
    "1 cup peanuts",
    "2 tablespoons unsalted butter, softened",
    "1 teaspoon baking soda"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Measure out all ingredients before starting. Grease a large rimmed baking sheet; set aside.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine sugar, corn syrup, water, and salt in a heavy, 2-quart saucepan over medium heat.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/xt7SJnHzGWDsNxnyOCqbGVvh9Yw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/15987-moms-best-peanut-brittle-ddmfs-step-1-0413-4x3-8fecf10c47a94cbeb29f986e284d8edf.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/15987/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir until sugar is completely dissolved and the mixture comes to a boil, about 5 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/xS53Ivp_NCOp1siWHgMf_dhcYz0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/15987-moms-best-peanut-brittle-ddmfs-step-3-0419-4x3-d0b5f03168e7464096ced87f35b586e2.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/15987/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir in peanuts and set a candy thermometer in place. Continue cooking, stirring occasionally, until the temperature reaches 300 to 310 degrees F (150 to 155 degrees C). Don't be tempted to stir too much as this can make the brittle turn grainy.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove from the heat. Quickly stir in butter and baking soda, then immediately pour mixture onto the prepared baking sheet. Quickly use 2 forks to lift and pull the mixture into a 12x14-inch rectangle. Let cool until completely firm, at least 30 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/G5gNESeGnszC3Wqaqs7QyfbaewY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/15987-moms-best-peanut-brittle-ddmfs-step-4-0426-4x3-aa31e6c4cb2b42a1b43ecca32b51e80b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/15987/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use a mallet to break peanut brittle into pieces.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/0FbsokejdgBIH1j4dah8_Bo87uU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/15987-moms-best-peanut-brittle-TheComfortofCooking-4x3-f0acb1417ef04435bd9f303c554b2006.jpg"
